DevOps Interview Preparation – Tool 4 

GitHub & GitHub Workflow (0–2 Years Experience)

GitHub is more than just code hosting.
For DevOps engineers, it’s the starting point of CI/CD, automation, and collaboration.

Interviewers expect you to understand how teams actually use GitHub.

📌 Focus: GitHub Interview Questions

• What is GitHub and how is it different from Git?
• What is a repository in GitHub?
• Difference between public and private repositories
• What is a fork? When do you use it?
• What is a Pull Request (PR)?
• PR vs Merge — what’s the difference?
• What are code reviews and why are they important?
• What is a GitHub issue?
• How do issues help in DevOps projects?
• What are GitHub labels and milestones?
• Explain GitHub workflow in a team environment
• What is a protected branch? Why is it used?
• What are GitHub webhooks?
• How does GitHub integrate with CI/CD tools?
• What are GitHub secrets and where are they used?
• Difference between GitHub Actions and Jenkins
• How do you secure credentials in GitHub?
• How do you manage multiple environments using GitHub?
• What is CODEOWNERS file?
• How do you revert a merged PR?
• Common GitHub mistakes beginners make
• Real-world GitHub workflow you followed in a project

💡 Interview Tip:
If you explain a simple flow like:

 “Developer → PR → Review → CI → Merge → Deploy”
you already sound like a working DevOps engineer.
